--- !u!114 &1338853155
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1338853153}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UnityEngine.UI::UnityEngine.UI.Text
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.88, g: 0.94, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 6e2084ce779d4ae4eb11312976664cdd, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 24
    m_FontStyle: 1
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 1
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 1
    m_LineSpacing: 1.4
  m_Text: 'A.X. 2347


    THE SPLICE PLAGUE



    Three decades ago the first outbreak
    turned

    the Meridian arcologies into hunting grounds.


    The infected
    do not die.

    They CHANGE.


    Werewolves. Chimeras. Reapers.

    Things
    with no names yet.



    Civilization survives behind blast-walls,

    and
    behind one name:


    SCEMATICA DYNAMICS


    The Corporation feeds the districts,
    mints

    the SCEMA scrip that pays for clean water

    and ammunition, and
    fields the only force

    that can answer an outbreak:


    THE GUN-HUNTERS


    You
    are one of them.



    Tonight, dispatch came down from Scematica

    tower:
    District 9 has gone dark. Outbreak-

    class signatures on every sensor.

    Civilians
    still inside.


    Your orders: descend into District 9,

    purge the infestation,
    and recover

    whatever the Corporation lost down there.



    They did not
    say what it was.


    They never do.'
